\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Apparatus architecture. The boundary condition input specifies the initial categorical state to be tested. The Field Configuration Unit (FPGA) imposes the chosen $\mathcal  {M}(\mathbf  {x},t)$ and $\mathbf  {A}_{\mathcal  {M}}$ on the substrate. The substrate hosts the four partition coordinates on its four oscillator channels. The symplectic integrator advances the state through the substrate at the clock rate. The completion detector identifies trajectory termination at a stable coordinate. The readout reports the completion coordinate as the detection event.}}{8}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:architecture}{{3}{8}{Apparatus architecture. The boundary condition input specifies the initial categorical state to be tested. The Field Configuration Unit (FPGA) imposes the chosen $\Depth (\mathbf {x},t)$ and $\Apartition $ on the substrate. The substrate hosts the four partition coordinates on its four oscillator channels. The symplectic integrator advances the state through the substrate at the clock rate. The completion detector identifies trajectory termination at a stable coordinate. The readout reports the completion coordinate as the detection event}{figure.3}{}}
